<Defs>

  <!--
    The Hollow Fleet (docs/design/peoples-third.md, the fourth of the eight; docs/design/peoples.md, "Release F";
    Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/PeoplesF2.cs): the crew of a colony ship that came down two hundred years ago and never
    flew again, still keeping its watches, ranks and logs in the grounded hull, still hoping to lift. Spacer, on the game's
    outlander parent; they arise in every age (ariseAges 0~3) and are at the height of the ages already (ageLimit 3; cut
    off from the world they fall back to the industrial age like any people). The ship's uniform for every rank, the
    uniform rule for a crew: a collar shirt and trousers in deck grey, worn and patched, the same on the captain as on the
    newest deckhand; the ship's guard add recon armour and charge rifles, the officers a jacket and, with Royalty, the
    beret of their rank, the captain a long coat. In another age the guard take the age's issue (ageArms: war shirts and
    spears among the tribes, plate and spears in the medieval age, flak and rifles in the industrial age). A share are
    mechanitors (Biotech's mechlink and headset) and psycasters (Royalty; Vanilla Psycasts Expanded's Skipmaster,
    Protector and Technomancer paths), and many are not baseliners at all, from the ship's long-ago gene work: starjacks
    (Odyssey), genies, highmates, hussars, Vanilla Races Expanded's archons and androids, Rimsenal's Åskbarns, Alpha Genes'
    nereids; deckhands with the ship's old gene work for health. Their towns are the grounded hull itself, with its landing
    pad and its hydroponics (Rimfolk_Plan_FleetHull). At the gate: a shuttle lands (Royalty's; else by drop pod) to trade
    spacer goods and a cryptosleep casket from the hull (Rimfolk_Evt_FleetShuttle); the Fleet buys the ship's chunks, persona
    cores and advanced components the colony salvages, its deckhands cutting the chunks apart where they lie
    (Rimfolk_Evt_FleetSalvage); a sleeper from their caskets, woken too late, asks the colony for shelter
    (Rimfolk_Evt_FleetSleeper). Their ask: plasteel and parts for the lift (Rimfolk_Mission_FleetLift). Their founding:
    Captain Imre Sallow's last order. Faith (Ideology): loyalty to the ship (loyalist), Odyssey's shipborn and the
    transhumanist's long-ago gene work.
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="OutlanderFactionBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_HollowFleet</defName>
    <label>Hollow Fleet</label>
    <description>The crew of a colony ship that came down two hundred years ago and never flew again. Their descendants still keep its watches, ranks and logs in the grounded hull, still stand their posts on decks that have not moved in generations, and still hope to lift. They come out to trade for the parts the ship needs and the salvage that falls from the sky, and they pay well for both.\n\nTheir ways began with the ship's last order. When the hull came down short of its world, Captain Imre Sallow told the crew to keep their posts until the order came to disembark, and then died before giving it. Nobody has had the rank to give it since, so the watches are still kept, the logs still written and the sleepers still sleep in their caskets below decks. Every member of the crew wears the ship's uniform in deck grey, patched by every generation that wore it before.\n\nThey are courteous, precise and a little sad, and they keep ship's time wherever they are. They fear the last part failing, a sleeper who wakes to strangers and the order that never comes. The hull is run by its first officer, and the Fleet by its captain.</description>
    <pawnSingular>crewman</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>crew</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>captain</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
