    <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
    <ideoName>The Ship's Watch</ideoName>
    <ideoDescription>The watch is kept until the order comes. Every member of the crew has a post and a rank, and the ship is everyone aboard it, the living, the sleepers in their caskets and the dead in the log. The body was made better before the voyage, as the ship was, and the crew keeps both in good repair. Captain Imre Sallow told the crew to keep their posts until the order came to disembark, and died before he could give it, so the ship's log has been written every day for two hundred years and still ends with the words "holding position".</ideoDescription>
