  <!-- ===================== Their people ===================== -->

  <!--
    How alike they look (docs/design/peoples.md, "Release F"): the ship's uniform for every rank (a crew, the uniform rule),
    only wear, quality and patches telling them apart: a collar shirt and trousers in deck grey on everyone. Deckhands
    wear over it whatever the hull's lockers held (the game's and the mods' everyday clothes, tool belts and packs); the
    ship's guard recon armour and helmet dyed the same grey, a smokepop or low-shield pack, charge rifles; the engineers
    Biotech's airwire headset over a mechlink; the officers a jacket and, with Royalty, the beret of their rank; the
    quartermaster and the captain a long coat (the captain with the beret too). In another age the guard take the age's
    issue (ageArms) in the same grey: war shirts and spears among the tribes, plate and spears in the medieval age, flak,
    helmets and assault rifles in the industrial age. A share of the officers and the captain are psycasters (Royalty;
    Vanilla Psycasts Expanded's Skipmaster, Protector and Technomancer), the engineers now and then A RimWorld of Magic's
    technomancers, a few deckhands carry the ship's old gene work for health (Biotech). They carry packaged meals, parts
    or medicine. Without any mod: the game's shirts, trousers, jackets, dusters, recon armour, charge rifles and pistols.
  -->
